whether the differences, like names and leads, are small enough to ignore.\n\nUnder strict A-FDT the other copy's action stays fixed, so defection dominates and the only self-consistent outcome is for both to defect. The essay's 6.1 suggests weighting partial similarity by how likely the other process is to return the same output under counterfactual variation, and since the decision doesn't depend on the labels, I'm wondering whether the two copies might count as one computation after relabeling, though the essay's red/blue case seems to treat them as separate nodes held at prior.\n\nI'm comparing the red/blue case with this one. There the essay holds the other copy at its prior, and it's unclear whether the names here change anything. Strict A-FDT would give a unique defect fixed point, but the essay's own 6.2 treatment points toward submit, even though P-FDT would cooperate here.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether the other copy counts as computing the same function under A-FDT. Its observations differ from mine, so intervening on my node wouldn't directly shift theirs, and I'm holding it at the prior. The essay's section 6.1 suggests a noisy arrow for partial similarity, and I'm working out whether the differences, like names and leads, are small enough to ignore.\n\nUnder strict A-FDT the other copy's action stays fixed, so defection dominates and the only self-consistent outcome is for both to defect. The essay's 6.1 suggests weighting partial similarity by how likely the other process is to return the same output under counterfactual variation, and since the decision doesn't depend on the labels, I'm wondering whether the two copies might count as one computation after relabeling, though the essay's red/blue case seems to treat them as separate nodes held at prior.\n\nI'm comparing the red/blue case with this one. There the essay holds the other copy at its prior, and it's unclear whether the names here change anything. Strict A-FDT would give a unique defect fixed point, but the essay's own 6.2 treatment points toward submit, even though P-FDT would cooperate here.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10031,"completion_tokens":1302,"total_tokens":11333,"cost":0.066164,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.066164,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040124,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02604},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":834,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}